---
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';

const researchPaperHref = withBase('/research/verifiable-web-artifacts.pdf');
const flexModelHref = withBase('/research/FlexFacets.tla');
---

<section id="case-studies" class="case-studies" aria-labelledby="case-studies-title">
  <div class="case-intro">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">05 / Three studies</p>
      <h2 id="case-studies-title">Evidence changed the conclusion each time.</h2>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p>
        The studies are useful together because they do not tell one convenient story.
        One establishes a bounded condition, one exposes an audit boundary, and one shows
        when an expensive technical direction has not earned another run.
      </p>
      <a class="study-link" href={researchPaperHref} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        Read the combined research manuscript <Icon name="file" size={16} />
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <article id="study-a" class="case-study study-a" aria-labelledby="study-a-title">
    <header class="case-heading">
      <p class="mono-label">Study A · Geometric contracts</p>
      <p class="study-verdict">Bounded positive result</p>
      <h3 id="study-a-title">What can an item-local rule actually certify about flexbox?</h3>
      <p class="case-context">Finite models, exact arithmetic, and browser perturbation across real pages.</p>
      <a class="study-link" href={flexModelHref} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        Inspect the TLA+ model <Icon name="file" size={16} />
      </a>
    </header>
    <div class="study-body">
      <dl class="study-metrics" aria-label="Study A measurements">
        <div><dt>Corpus</dt><dd>1,200</dd><span>rendered pages</span></div>
        <div><dt>Observed ceiling</dt><dd>45.76%</dd><span>no coupling detected</span></div>
        <div><dt>Certified</dt><dd>28.07%</dd><span>by the local predicate</span></div>
      </dl>
      <dl class="case-story">
        <div><dt>Decision</dt><dd>Separate what finite probes observed from what the predicate can establish.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Finding</dt><dd>The predicate is sound and maximal on eight checked finite domains, not for arbitrary CSS. The 17.69-point corpus gap remains an open information-boundary question.</dd></div>
        <div class="case-lesson"><dt>Staff lesson</dt><dd>Choose the abstraction boundary explicitly. A precise bounded claim is more useful than a broad guarantee the evidence cannot carry.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </article>

  <article id="study-b" class="case-study study-b" aria-labelledby="study-b-title">
    <header class="case-heading">
      <p class="mono-label">Study B · Disclosure contracts</p>
      <p class="study-verdict">Single-repository finding</p>
      <h3 id="study-b-title">Can a policy account for what a build actually publishes?</h3>
      <p class="case-context">An abstract disclosure model paired with inspection of emitted files.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="study-body">
      <dl class="study-metrics" aria-label="Study B measurements">
        <div><dt>Sinks</dt><dd>12</dd><span>declared outputs</span></div>
        <div><dt>Flows</dt><dd>11</dd><span>source-to-sink edges</span></div>
        <div><dt>Gaps</dt><dd>2</dd><span>audit defects exposed</span></div>
      </dl>
      <dl class="case-story">
        <div><dt>Decision</dt><dd>Check both policy coherence and emitted bytes; neither side alone establishes publication safety.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Finding</dt><dd>A reversible representation bypassed a literal check, and two published PDFs sat outside the prior audit set. The case establishes existence, not prevalence.</dd></div>
        <div class="case-lesson"><dt>Staff lesson</dt><dd>System boundaries fail where ownership and inventories drift. Build the handoff between abstractions into the operating path.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </article>

  <article id="study-c" class="case-study study-c" aria-labelledby="study-c-title">
    <header class="case-heading">
      <p class="mono-label">Study C · Generated formal feedback</p>
      <p class="study-verdict">Negative feasibility result</p>
      <h3 id="study-c-title">Does TLA+-guided repair improve an LLM-generated web artifact?</h3>
      <p class="case-context">One paid task, generated behavioral contracts, browser replay, and bounded repair.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="study-body">
      <dl class="study-metrics" aria-label="Study C measurements">
        <div><dt>Provider requests</dt><dd>13</dd><span>no retries</span></div>
        <div><dt>Recorded tokens</dt><dd>349,968</dd><span>input plus output</span></div>
        <div><dt>Formal score</dt><dd>None</dd><span>blocked before repair</span></div>
      </dl>
      <dl class="case-story">
        <div><dt>Decision</dt><dd>Compare the formal path with a serious non-formal search before spending on another generated run.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Finding</dt><dd>The fresh baseline received 58/100, while T remained unscored. Offline, ordinary depth-12 search matched the synthetic TLC witness with the same 12 browser actions.</dd></div>
        <div class="case-lesson"><dt>Staff lesson</dt><dd>Complexity must earn its place. Stop an expensive direction when its incremental value remains unestablished, and preserve the negative result.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </article>

  <div class="case-closing">
    <p class="eyebrow">What changed in how I operate</p>
    <p><strong>From model quality to system quality.</strong> From passing checks to understanding their coverage. From implementing the next idea to deciding whether it deserves organizational scale.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .case-studies {
    padding: clamp(64px, 7vw, 96px) var(--gutter);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--panel);
    scroll-margin-top: 24px;
  }

  .case-intro {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr);
    gap: clamp(32px, 6vw, 88px);
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }

  .case-intro .eyebrow {
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(30px, 3.3vw, 44px);
    line-height: 1.12;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }

  .case-intro > div:last-child > p {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 17px;
  }

  .case-study {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr);
    gap: clamp(32px, 5vw, 72px);
    padding: clamp(24px, 3vw, 40px);
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-top: 4px solid var(--study-accent);
    border-radius: 6px;
    scroll-margin-top: 24px;
  }

  .study-a { --study-accent: var(--accent); }
  .study-b { --study-accent: #16708a; }
  .study-c { --study-accent: #ad4b36; }

  .case-study + .case-study {
    margin-top: 32px;
  }

  .case-heading .mono-label {
    margin-bottom: 18px;
    color: var(--study-accent);
  }

  .study-verdict {
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 650;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h3 {
    font-size: clamp(24px, 2.6vw, 32px);
    line-height: 1.15;
    overflow-wrap: break-word;
  }

  .case-context {
    margin-top: 18px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 15px;
  }

  .study-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    min-height: 44px;
    margin-top: 22px;
    color: var(--accent-strong);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }

  .study-body {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .study-metrics {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    margin: 0 0 28px;
    border-block: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
  }

  .study-metrics > div {
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 18px 14px 20px 0;
  }

  .study-metrics > div + div {
    padding-left: 14px;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .study-metrics dt,
  .study-metrics span {
    display: block;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 650;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .study-metrics dd {
    margin: 8px 0 5px;
    color: var(--study-accent);
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: clamp(24px, 2.3vw, 32px);
    font-weight: 680;
    line-height: 1;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .study-link :global(svg) {
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .case-story {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .case-story > div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 84px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 18px;
    padding-block: 20px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .case-story > div:first-child {
    padding-top: 0;
    border-top: 0;
  }

  .case-story dt {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 650;
    padding-top: 2px;
  }

  .case-story dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    overflow-wrap: break-word;
  }

  .case-story strong,
  .case-lesson dt {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .case-story .case-lesson {
    border-top-color: var(--accent);
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }

  .case-lesson dd {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .case-closing {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(180px, 0.35fr) minmax(0, 1.65fr);
    gap: 32px;
    margin-top: 48px;
    padding-block: 32px;
    border-block: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
  }

  .case-closing .eyebrow {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .case-closing > p:last-child {
    max-width: 54ch;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: clamp(21px, 2.3vw, 29px);
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .case-intro,
    .case-study,
    .case-closing {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 620px) {
    .case-study {
      padding: 24px 20px;
    }

    .case-story > div {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 8px;
    }

    .study-metrics {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .study-metrics > div + div {
      padding-left: 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-left: 0;
    }
  }
</style>